---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
// Converted from the OKAD case artifact. Styles are scoped under .case-designed.
const title = "Two creams. A Walmart launch. Not one new shoot. | OKAD Agency";
const description = "ZenToes was launching two foot creams at Walmart and needed ads fast. Instead of booking creators, we logged every clip the brand already had, wrote ads around what was really on camera and edited them into a full test batch.";
const ogImage = "/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-01.jpg";
---

<Base title={title} description={description} ogImage={ogImage}>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Instrument+Serif:ital@0;1&family=Reenie+Beanie&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="case-designed">






<!-- COVER -->
<section class="cover">
  <div class="w">
    <div class="cover-grid">
      <div class="stack" style="gap:24px">
        <span class="kick">Foot care · Retail launch at Walmart</span>
        <h1>Two creams. A Walmart launch. <span class="cap g">Not one new shoot.</span></h1>
        <p class="lead">ZenToes was launching two foot creams at Walmart and needed ads fast. Instead of booking creators, we logged every clip the brand already had, wrote ads around what was really on camera and edited them into a full test batch.</p>
        <div class="meta">
          <div><b>April 2026</b><span>Walmart launch batch</span></div>
          <div><b>2 products</b><span>Magnesium Sleep and 40% Urea foot creams</span></div>
          <div><b>Our scope</b><span>Footage audit, concepts, hooks, scripts, editing, static ads</span></div>
          <div><b>Not our scope</b><span>Filming and media buying: footage came from the brand's library</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="collage" aria-label="Frames from the ads">
        <div class="ann hand" style="right:-6px;top:-74px">real frames from the ads<svg width="70" height="60" viewBox="0 0 70 60"><path d="M6 6 C 34 2, 56 18, 60 52"/><path d="M51 44 L60 54 L66 42"/></svg></div>
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="POV 2AM closing shift hook" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-01.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Cream in a Walmart cart" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-02.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Creator holding the Urea cream" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-03.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Ballerina in the studio" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-04.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Bare foot on the beach" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-05.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Cream found on a Walmart shelf" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-06.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Husband talking about the cream" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-07.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Applying cream in the bedroom" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-08.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="strip">
      <div><b>11</b><span>videos edited for the launch</span></div>
      <div><b>14</b><span>static ads alongside them</span></div>
      <div><b>16+</b><span>concepts with hooks, shot lists and scripts</span></div>
      <div><b>0</b><span>new shoots, castings or product shipments</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="howto"><span><b>Hook</b> = the first seconds that make people stop scrolling.</span><span><b>B-roll</b> = footage that plays under the voice or text.</span><span><b>Concept</b> = one ad idea: angle, hook, shots and script.</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Q1 -->
<section>
  <div class="w two">
    <div class="stack">
      <span class="q-kick">Q1 · Why not just shoot new content?</span>
      <h2>Because the footage <span class="cap p">was already there.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">The brand had folders of creator videos from earlier campaigns: bedroom routines, a ballerina, cracked-heel demos, clips filmed in Walmart. Nobody had looked at them as raw material for new ads. A launch can't wait for casting, shipping and reshoots.</p>
      <p class="pro"><b>For marketers</b>Reusing licensed UGC as b-roll cuts cost and time per ad; the bottleneck moves from production to ideas.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="before-after">
      <div class="box before">
        <span class="tag">What we got</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Creator clips from past campaigns</li>
          <li>Product photos: studio, flatlay, shelf</li>
          <li>Two creams with different jobs</li>
          <li>A launch date at Walmart</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="box dark">
        <span class="tag g">The brief</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Ads for both creams, existing footage only</li>
          <li>Voiceover and music-plus-text videos</li>
          <li>Static ads alongside the videos</li>
          <li>Every ad ends at the Walmart shelf</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Q2 -->
<section>
  <div class="w">
    <div class="stack">
      <span class="q-kick">Q2 · How do you find ads inside old footage?</span>
      <h2>We logged every shot <span class="cap g">before writing a line.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">Every clip got a code and a one-line description: M for Magnesium, U for Urea, L for lifestyle. That catalog became the alphabet. A concept could only use shots that exist, so nothing written on paper fell apart in the edit.</p>
      <p class="pro"><b>For marketers</b>64 shot codes across 10 creators. Each concept lists its b-roll sequence by code, with a note on why every shot is there.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sources">
      <div class="box"><span class="tag g">1 · We log</span><h3>Every shot, coded</h3><p>Who, where, what happens and how close: product close-ups, applications, "before" feet, store moments.</p></div>
      <div class="box"><span class="tag g">2 · We match</span><h3>Footage to feelings</h3><p>A dancer leaving the studio reads as "end of a long shift". A woman doing chores reads as "she never sits down".</p></div>
      <div class="box"><span class="tag g">3 · We write</span><h3>Scripts to the shot list</h3><p>Every line of voiceover lands on a shot that shows it, so the picture never argues with the words.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="insights">
      <div class="ins">
        <div class="quote">Takes the cream off a Walmart shelf, scans it at checkout.<small>WHAT WAS ON CAMERA</small></div>
        <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="64" height="24" viewBox="0 0 64 24"><path d="M3 14 C 20 9, 40 16, 58 11"/><path d="M50 4 L59 11 L50 18"/></svg></div>
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Cream held up at the Walmart shelf" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-06.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <p><b>Became "the $9.99 Walmart find".</b> A discovery ad where the price is the hook and the shelf is the proof that you can buy it today.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ins dark">
        <div class="quote">A ballerina at the barre, then walking out tired.<small>ONE CREATOR, STUDIO TO HOME</small></div>
        <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="64" height="24" viewBox="0 0 64 24"><path d="M3 14 C 20 9, 40 16, 58 11"/><path d="M50 4 L59 11 L50 18"/></svg></div>
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Ballerina sitting by the barre" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-04.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <p><b>Became ads for anyone on their feet all day.</b> Dancers, nurses, servers: the studio stands in for every long shift.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ins">
        <div class="quote">A man on the couch, showing the tube.<small>A CLIP NOBODY HAD A USE FOR</small></div>
        <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="64" height="24" viewBox="0 0 64 24"><path d="M3 14 C 20 9, 40 16, 58 11"/><path d="M50 4 L59 11 L50 18"/></svg></div>
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Husband talking about the cream" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-07.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <p><b>Became "my husband stole my foot cream".</b> Humour plus social proof: if he uses it after the gym, it's more than a pampering product. The ad ends on "buy two".</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Q3 -->
<section>
  <div class="w">
    <div class="stack">
      <span class="q-kick">Q3 · Two creams in one batch?</span>
      <h2>Two products, <span class="cap g">two different jobs.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">The Magnesium cream sells a feeling: tired feet and better sleep. The Urea cream sells a visible fix: cracked heels, smooth again. So each got its own angles, its own footage and its own kind of proof.</p>
      <p class="pro"><b>For marketers</b>Every concept was pre-scored 1–10 on hook strength, watch-through and purchase intent to set the order of the edit queue.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prod">
      <div class="box dark"><span class="tag g dewtag">Magnesium Sleep</span>
        <ul class="hook-list">
          <li>On your feet all day <span>dancers, shifts</span></li>
          <li>The 2-minute bedtime ritual <span>sleep</span></li>
          <li>Magnesium on your feet, not in a pill <span>education</span></li>
          <li>My husband stole my foot cream <span>humour</span></li>
          <li>She hasn't sat down since 6am <span>moms</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="box plain"><span class="tag">40% Urea</span>
        <ul class="hook-list">
          <li>I haven't shown my feet in three years <span>shame</span></li>
          <li>I threw away my pumice stone <span>switch</span></li>
          <li>$400 on pedicures, cracked every time <span>money</span></li>
          <li>What 4 weeks did to my heels <span>before / after</span></li>
          <li>The concentration podiatrists use <span>authority</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <details class="more"><summary>See the concept list</summary>
    <div class="mx-wrap">
      <table class="mx">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Concept</th><th scope="col">Cream</th><th scope="col">Format</th><th scope="col">Hook (shortened)</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>The Sandal Confession</td><td>Urea</td><td>Voiceover</td><td class="h">"I returned sandals three times this year. Not because of the fit."</td></tr>
          <tr><td>The 12-Hour Shift</td><td>Magnesium</td><td>Voiceover</td><td class="h">"Nurses, servers, dancers: if your feet throb after you sit down, watch this."</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Husband Stole It</td><td>Magnesium</td><td>Voiceover</td><td class="h">"I need to file a complaint. My husband stole my foot cream."</td></tr>
          <tr><td>60 Seconds</td><td>Urea</td><td>Voiceover</td><td class="h">"I threw away my pumice stone. Here's what replaced it."</td></tr>
          <tr><td>On Your Feet</td><td>Magnesium</td><td>Voiceover</td><td class="h">"Everyone's taking magnesium pills. Nobody's putting it on their feet."</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2-Minute Reset</td><td>Magnesium</td><td>Music + text</td><td class="h">"the 2-minute foot ritual that replaced my sleeping pills"</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Week by Week</td><td>Urea</td><td>Music + text</td><td class="h">"what 4 weeks of 40% urea did to my heels"</td></tr>
          <tr><td>The Walmart Find</td><td>Magnesium</td><td>Music + text</td><td class="h">"the $9.99 Walmart find that fixed my sleep"</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Chaos vs Calm</td><td>Magnesium</td><td>Music + text</td><td class="h">"she hasn't sat down since 6am"</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Closing Shift</td><td>Magnesium</td><td>Voiceover</td><td class="h">"2AM. Closing shift done. My feet are on fire."</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Dance Bag</td><td>Magnesium</td><td>Voiceover</td><td class="h">"The one thing that's always in my dance bag. Not tape."</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Studio to Sheets</td><td>Magnesium</td><td>Music + text</td><td class="h">"6 hours on pointe. this is what saves my feet."</td></tr>
          <tr><td colspan="4" style="color:var(--soft);font-weight:400">+ character stories and 10 static concepts with headline, copy and CTA</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    </details>
    <div class="chips">
      <span class="chip"><b>16+</b> video concepts</span>
      <span class="chip"><b>3</b> hook options per voiceover script</span>
      <span class="chip"><b>3</b> lines max on screen per music video</span>
      <span class="chip"><b>10</b> static concepts</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Q4 FORMATS -->
<section class="dew">
  <div class="w">
    <div class="stack">
      <span class="q-kick">Q4 · Which formats?</span>
      <h2>Four ways to tell it, <span class="cap g">tested side by side.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">The same footage can carry a spoken story, a silent text ad, a whole persona or a meme. Running them together shows which language the audience answers to, not just which clip.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="fmt-grid">
      <div class="fmt"><figure class="ph"><img alt="Urea cream held to camera" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-03.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure><span class="lbl native">Voiceover</span><h3>A first-person story</h3><p>25–40 s over b-roll, written word for word and ready to record.</p></div>
      <div class="fmt"><figure class="ph"><img alt="Applying cream on the bed" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-08.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure><span class="lbl native">Music + text</span><h3>No voice, three lines</h3><p>Lo-fi or trending audio; on-screen text carries the whole story.</p></div>
      <div class="fmt"><figure class="ph"><img alt="Ballerina in the studio" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-04.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure><span class="lbl proof">Character</span><h3>One creator, one life</h3><p>The dancer, the mom, the night-shift worker: one person's clips become a persona.</p></div>
      <div class="fmt"><figure class="ph"><img alt="POV husband hook in the cart" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-02.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure><span class="lbl proof">POV hook</span><h3>Meme first, product second</h3><p>"POV: your husband steals your foot cream." Looks native to the feed.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Q5 -->
<section>
  <div class="w">
    <div class="stack">
      <span class="q-kick">Q5 · Who is each ad for?</span>
      <h2>Every ad talks to <span class="cap p">someone who knows the pain.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">"Foot cream" is not an audience. People who stand ten hours a day are, and so are people who stopped wearing sandals. Each concept picks one of them and says it in their words.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cast three">
      <div class="person">
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Ballerina" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-04.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <div class="stack" style="gap:6px"><span class="kick">Magnesium</span><h3>Dancers</h3><ul><li>6 hours on pointe</li><li>Lives in the dance bag</li><li>Arnica after class</li></ul></div>
      </div>
      <div class="person">
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Night-shift creator with cream" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-01.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <div class="stack" style="gap:6px"><span class="kick">Magnesium</span><h3>Shift workers</h3><ul><li>2AM, closing shift</li><li>Concrete floors, no sitting</li><li>On the nightstand tonight</li></ul></div>
      </div>
      <div class="person">
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Bare feet on the beach" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-09.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <div class="stack" style="gap:6px"><span class="kick">40% Urea</span><h3>Heel hiders</h3><ul><li>3 years, no sandals</li><li>Pumice that never worked</li><li>The beach as the payoff</li></ul></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Q6 BEATS -->
<section class="dew">
  <div class="w two">
    <div class="stack">
      <span class="q-kick">Q6 · How is one ad built?</span>
      <h2>Five beats, <span class="cap g">ending at the shelf.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">Short ads leave no room to wander. Every script follows the same skeleton, so a viewer gets the pain, the reason it works and where to buy it before the music ends.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="stack">
      <div class="hooks">
        <div class="box dark"><span class="tag g dewtag">Details we used</span>
          <ul class="hook-list">
            <li>Bled through my socks last July</li>
            <li>Clogs off, feet don't fit back in</li>
            <li>He has his own tube on his side of the bed</li>
            <li>One tube, still not empty</li>
            <li>Cheaper than the dog's treats</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="box plain"><span class="tag">Checked before sending</span>
          <ul class="hook-list">
            <li>Every line has a real shot</li>
            <li>One cream, one promise</li>
            <li>Price and store at the end</li>
            <li>Three lines max on screen</li>
            <li>"Helps ease", never "cures"</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="w">
    <div class="timeline" aria-label="Ad structure">
      <div><span class="s">beat 1</span><b>Hook</b><span class="q">"POV: you finally stop hiding your feet"</span></div>
      <div><span class="s">beat 2</span><b>The pain</b><span class="q">"Cracked heels for 3 years. No sandals, no pedicures."</span></div>
      <div><span class="s">beat 3</span><b>Why it works</b><span class="q">"40% Urea works through the cracks, not just the surface."</span></div>
      <div><span class="s">beat 4</span><b>Proof</b><span class="q">"2 weeks. Ran my finger across, smooth."</span></div>
      <div><span class="s">beat 5</span><b>Price + place</b><span class="q">"$9.99 at Walmart. Lasts up to 4 months."</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Q7 GAPS -->
<section>
  <div class="w">
    <div class="stack">
      <span class="q-kick">Q7 · What if the footage doesn't fit?</span>
      <h2>We flagged the gaps <span class="cap y">instead of faking them.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">A fixed library means some ideas hit missing shots. Every concept was marked before editing, so the client saw upfront which ones were ready and which needed a workaround.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rule-row">
      <div class="box"><span class="tag">Green or amber</span><h3>Ready vs needs a fix</h3><p>Green concepts went straight to the edit. Amber ones carried a note: which shot is missing and what replaces it.</p></div>
      <div class="box"><span class="tag">Burned-in text</span><h3>Captions on captions</h3><p>Some lifestyle clips already had subtitles. New text sits on a solid background so the two never fight.</p></div>
      <div class="box"><span class="tag">Missing shots</span><h3>Swap, don't stretch</h3><p>No office desk, no kitchen floor at 2AM. We used the closest real shot or moved the idea into a static ad.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="hn" style="justify-content:flex-end;margin-top:14px"><svg style="transform:scaleX(-1)" width="60" height="46" viewBox="0 0 60 46"><path d="M4 42 C 26 42, 34 10, 54 6"/><path d="M45 1 L55 6 L47 13"/></svg><span class="hand">no surprises in the edit</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Q8 WALMART -->
<section>
  <div class="w">
    <div class="stack">
      <span class="q-kick">Q8 · Why is Walmart in every ad?</span>
      <h2>The store is <span class="cap g">part of the proof.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">For a launch, "where do I get it" matters as much as "why". Shelf, cart and storefront shots turn $9.99 into a reason to try it today, not a reason to add it to a wishlist.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="reel">
      <figure class="ph"><img alt="On the shelf" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-06.jpg" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Found on the shelf</figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="ph"><img alt="In the cart" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-02.jpg" loading="lazy"><figcaption>In the cart</figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="ph"><img alt="Outside the store" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-10.jpg" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Outside the store</figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="ph"><img alt="Price on screen" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-11.jpg" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Price on screen</figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="ph"><img alt="On the nightstand" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-12.jpg" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Home on the nightstand</figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="ph"><img alt="Both creams" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-13.jpg" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Both creams, one routine</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<!-- STATICS -->
<section class="dew">
  <div class="w">
    <div class="stack">
      <span class="q-kick">Q9 · And the static ads?</span>
      <h2>Same ideas, <span class="cap g">no video needed.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">Statics carry the angles that work in one glance: before and after, a price, a meme. They also caught the ideas that had no footage: the corporate-girl concept had no office shots, so it became a starter-pack static instead of a weak video.</p>
      <p class="pro"><b>For marketers</b>Each static mirrors a video angle, so a winning message can be confirmed across formats, not just in one creative.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sgrid">
      <figure><img alt="Review with before and after heels" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-14.jpg" loading="lazy"><figcaption><b>Review + before/after</b>Urea · a customer quote does the selling</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img alt="You were on your feet for 14 hours" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-15.jpg" loading="lazy"><figcaption><b>14 hours on your feet</b>Magnesium · the shift-worker angle</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img alt="60 seconds before bed, before and after" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-16.jpg" loading="lazy"><figcaption><b>60 seconds before bed</b>Urea · the ritual, with proof</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img alt="End-of-day foot relief only 9.99" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-17.jpg" loading="lazy"><figcaption><b>$9.99 relief</b>Magnesium · price and store up front</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img alt="Corporate girl starter pack" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-18.jpg" loading="lazy"><figcaption><b>Corporate girl starter pack</b>Magnesium · the idea with no office footage</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img alt="Smooth heels aren't luck" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-19.jpg" loading="lazy"><figcaption><b>Smooth heels aren't luck</b>Urea · ingredients as the reason</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img alt="You stand for 12 hours" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-20.jpg" loading="lazy"><figcaption><b>You stand for 12 hours</b>Magnesium · creator frames in a collage</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img alt="Tired feet after a long day" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-21.jpg" loading="lazy"><figcaption><b>Tired feet after a long day?</b>Magnesium · question hook</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
    <div class="vwrap">
      <div class="vbox four">
        <span class="tag hand-lbl">one message, four layouts</span>
        <div class="vgrid">
          <figure><img alt="This is not dry skin, variant A" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-22.jpg" loading="lazy"><figcaption>A</figcaption></figure>
          <figure><img alt="This is not dry skin, variant B" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-23.jpg" loading="lazy"><figcaption>B</figcaption></figure>
          <figure><img alt="This is not dry skin, variant C" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-24.jpg" loading="lazy"><figcaption>C</figcaption></figure>
          <figure><img alt="This is not dry skin, variant D" src="/images/cases/zentoes-walmart-launch-ads/img-25.jpg" loading="lazy"><figcaption>D</figcaption></figure>
        </div>
        <p>"This is NOT dry skin": the same explanation of why cracks come back, tested in four layouts and colour schemes, so the test reads design, not message.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vbox two">
        <span class="tag hand-lbl">two backgrounds</span>
